                <pb facs="0535" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/136: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Bilbao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapman</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-04T13:00:00+01:00">July 4, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 4—11:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram No. B–203, June 14, 2 p.m. Spanish Consul at Hendaye called
                    July 2nd to discuss question of admission of 500 Basque children, all under 16,
                    into the United States. He has since furnished a letter showing the children are
                    still to be evacuated which doubtless means Basque children from Bilbao now at
                    Santander. I have furnished Consul General outline legal requirements to be met
                    reserving the right to determine each individual case upon its legal merits.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
